{"id":29650,"slug":"a-tale-of-summer","title":"A Tale of Summer","year":1996,"country":"France","duration":114,"spine":null,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/29650-a-tale-of-summer","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/8b60c1bafaf12fda5a8751aaec6c250f/IERWWzxewKNIcG02bBeaMFkZVuM01Z_large.jpg","description":"According to Eric Rohmer, A Tale of Summer is the most autobiographical film that he made. Based on events from Rohmer’s youth, this installment of Tales of the Four Seasons follows amateur musician Gaspard (Melvil Poupaud) to a seaside resort in Dinard, on the coast of Brittany. There, three women (Amanda Langlet, Gwenaëlle Simon, and Aurélia Nolin) each offer the possibility of romance, but Gaspard’s inability to commit to just one puts all of his chances at love in jeopardy. The film features Rohmer’s wistful observations on indecisiveness and the fickle nature of desire, as brought to life by a talented young cast in a picturesque setting.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Eric Rohmer","slug":"eric-rohmer"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Melvil Poupaud","role":"Gaspard","slug":"melvil-poupaud"},{"actor":"Amanda Langlet","role":"Margot","slug":"amanda-langlet"},{"actor":"Gwenaëlle Simon","role":"Solène","slug":"gwenaelle-simon"},{"actor":"Aurélia Nolin","role":"Léna","slug":"aurelia-nolin"},{"actor":"Aimé Lefèvre","role":"The Newfoundlander","slug":"aime-lefevre"},{"actor":"Alain Guellaff","role":"Uncle Alan","slug":"alain-guellaff"},{"actor":"Evelyne Lahana","role":"Aunt Maiwen","slug":"evelyne-lahana"},{"actor":"Yves Guérin","role":"Accordion player","slug":"yves-guerin"},{"actor":"Franck Cabot-David","role":"The cousin","slug":"franck-cabot-david"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Eric Rohmer","slug":"eric-rohmer"},{"role":"Written by","person":"Eric Rohmer","slug":"eric-rohmer"},{"role":"Producer","person":"Margaret Ménégoz","slug":null},{"role":"Producer","person":"Les Films du Losange","slug":null},{"role":"Producer",